    "answer": {
      "short": "The power law: $\\log(a^n)=n\\log(a)$.",
      "worked": "The logarithmic power law brings the exponent outside the logarithm:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log(a^n)&=n\\log(a).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
